 CellChangeTimes->{{3.988201532003448*^9, 
  3.988201536787407*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"f9796ecd-52dc-44b1-ab3d-\
d7cdf3ebc678"],

Cell["\<\
Department of Chemistry and Biochemistry
Western Kentucky University
Bowling Green, KY 42101-1079
Email: jeremy.maddox@wku.edu\
\>", "Affiliation",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.988201549259402*^9, 
  3.988201579115401*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"b7217d74-bf0b-4029-8ac3-\
c812a0d96213"],

Cell["\<\
The GWPEnsemble package provides a self-contained framework for generating, \
propagating, and post-processing quantum trajectory ensembles within \
GWPTools. Given a GWPObject across the \[OpenCurlyDoubleQuote]1D\
\[CloseCurlyDoubleQuote], \
\[OpenCurlyDoubleQuote]SS1D\[CloseCurlyDoubleQuote], \
\[OpenCurlyDoubleQuote]MC1D\[CloseCurlyDoubleQuote], or \
\[OpenCurlyDoubleQuote]2D\[CloseCurlyDoubleQuote] wavepacket engines, \
GWPEnsemble constructs structured initial coordinate grids using exact \
inverse-CDF quantile mapping, uniform spatial discretization, or Monte Carlo \
importance sampling. For time-dependent propagation, GWPEnsembleSolve \
integrates first-order kinematic (Bohmian guidance) or second-order dynamic \
(Newton\[Dash]Bohm) equations of motion\[LongDash]either directly from a \
GWPObject or through user-supplied velocity and acceleration \
fields\[LongDash]while GWPEnsembleParse and GWPEnsembleFormat extract the \
underlying InterpolatingFunction time grids and reshape the resulting \
trajectory and derivative tensors for visualization and phase-space analysis.\
\
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{4.002128701193407*^9, 
  4.002233619968487*^9},ExpressionUUID->"63012113-dbab-4e8d-bb28-\
20848d1967b2"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["Loading the package", "Section",
 CellChangeTimes->{{4.0021286565359697`*^9, 
  4.002128659011773*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"9a3f4dcc-9220-432c-97bd-\
51d8441b867f"],

Cell["\<\
Load the core GWPTools package along with the engine, hydrodynamics, \
numerical potential, and GWPEnsemble extensions. (During active repository \
development, PacletDirectoryLoad points directly to the local working tree \
and is omitted once the compiled v1.0.1 paclet is installed.)\
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{4.002128716885373*^9, 
  4.0022340627668447`*^9},ExpressionUUID->"46502e3b-9a3f-47fb-8b62-\
8a9a1ee25a1f"],

